Carried patch, Windows only: regression cases stage copies, not symlinks.

ScopedExampleStage in test/unit/regression_helpers.cpp stages each regression
case by symlinking every entry of its input directory into a fresh directory
and running Palace there. MinGW's libstdc++ has no symlink() and always fails,
so every regression case would fail to stage on Windows. On _WIN32 each entry
is copied instead (recursively, for the mesh/ directories). The inputs are the
installed test data, where upstream's install already dereferences the source
tree's symlinks, so the copy is of real files. Linux and macOS stage as before.

diff --git a/test/unit/regression_helpers.cpp b/test/unit/regression_helpers.cpp
index 2ebc3e7..2378b38 100644
--- a/test/unit/regression_helpers.cpp
+++ b/test/unit/regression_helpers.cpp
@@ -342,7 +342,13 @@ public:
         {
           continue;
         }
+#if defined(_WIN32)
+        // MinGW's libstdc++ cannot create symlinks, so stage a copy.
+        std::filesystem::copy(entry.path(), stage_ / name,
+                              std::filesystem::copy_options::recursive, ec);
+#else
         std::filesystem::create_symlink(entry.path(), stage_ / name, ec);
+#endif
         if (ec)
         {
           ok = 0;
